c-arbint 0.0.2 (2026-02-10)
===========================

Second development release. Major feature additions across the board: random
number generation, cryptographic hashing, bitwise operations, shift operations,
exponentiation, integer square root, multi-limb division via Knuth Algorithm D,
and optimized squaring. The public API grows from ~139 to ~158 functions.

New Features
------------
- Random number generation (arbint_rng_t):
  * Mersenne Twister (MT19937) seeded from platform entropy
  * arbint_urandomb: uniform random in [0, 2^k)
  * arbint_urandomm: uniform random in [0, bound) via rejection sampling
  * Platform entropy: BCryptGenRandom (Windows), arc4random_buf (macOS/BSD),
    /dev/urandom (Linux/POSIX)
  * Configurable via --disable-entropy for embedded targets

- Cryptographic hashing:
  * arbint_hash_slow: SHA-256-based variable-length hash
  * arbint_hash_fast: CRC32C-based 32-bit hash for hash tables
  * Counter-mode construction for arbitrary output lengths

- Bitwise operations (two's-complement semantics):
  * arbint_and, arbint_or, arbint_xor, arbint_not
  * Scalar variants: arbint_{and,or,xor}_{i32,u32}
  * arbint_testbit, arbint_setbit, arbint_clrbit
  * arbint_popcount, arbint_hammingdist, arbint_ctz, arbint_clz

- Shift operations:
  * arbint_shl: left shift (rop = a * 2^k)
  * arbint_shr: right shift truncating toward zero

- Size queries:
  * arbint_nbits: number of significant bits
  * arbint_sizeinbase: digit count in base 2-62 (fixed-point reciprocal LUT)

- Exponentiation:
  * arbint_pow_u32: base^exp via right-to-left binary exponentiation

- Integer square root:
  * arbint_isqrt: floor(sqrt(a)) via Newton's method with quadratic convergence

- Multi-limb division via Knuth Algorithm D:
  * Replaces the O(n^2 * bits) binary long-division algorithm
  * O(n * m) for n-limb / m-limb division
  * Reciprocal-based quotient estimation with Knuth's correction step

- Optimized squaring:
  * Dedicated Karatsuba and naive squaring paths (separate from multiplication)
  * Shared core via arbint_mul_core.inc template

- Declared (not yet implemented) number-theoretic stubs in arbint.h:
  * arbint_moebius, arbint_totient, arbint_carmichael
  * arbint_is_square, arbint_is_power, arbint_root
  * arbint_isprime, arbint_inv_mod, arbint_inv_mod_u32

Performance Optimizations
-------------------------
- Default optimization level raised from -O2 to -O3
- -fno-semantic-interposition enabled where supported (shared library speedup)
- x86 POPCNT intrinsics for arbint_popcount/arbint_hammingdist (8+ limbs)
- SHA-NI hardware acceleration for SHA-256 (Intel Goldmont+, AMD Zen+)
- SSE4.2 hardware acceleration for CRC32C
- Knuth Algorithm D dramatically improves large-number division throughput

New Platform Support
--------------------
- AArch64 (ARM64) hardware acceleration framework:
  * Runtime feature detection via getauxval (Linux)
  * ARM CRC32 + PMULL for CRC32C acceleration
  * ARM SHA-2 crypto extensions for SHA-256 acceleration
  * NEON SIMD support infrastructure

Build System
------------
- New autoconf macros: ARBINT_CHECK_ARM_FEATURE_WITH_FLAG (m4/arbint_arm_feature_check.m4)
- POPCNT, SHA-NI, SSE4.2 CRC32, ARM CRC32, ARM PMULL, ARM SHA-2 feature detection
- --disable-entropy configure option for environments without entropy sources
- Detection of explicit_bzero/memset_s for secure memory zeroing
- Improved release signing script (armored signatures, bundled archives)

Testing
-------
- 7 new test binaries: test_random, test_hash, test_shift, test_bitops,
  test_pow, test_isqrt, test_sqr, test_mul_exhaustive
- 2 new example programs: compute_e (e to 10000 digits), compute_bitops
- Total: 17 test/example binaries (up from 8)

Documentation
-------------
- Man page expanded with documentation for all new APIs
- README converted to Markdown (README.md)

Known Limitations
-----------------
- String conversion (arbint_set_str, arbint_get_str) not yet implemented
- Floor/ceiling division variants planned for future releases
- Number-theoretic functions (primality, totient, etc.) declared but not yet
  implemented


c-arbint 0.0.1 (2026-02-08)
===========================

Initial public release of c-arbint, a portable arbitrary-precision integer
library for C with a focus on performance optimization and clean API design.

Core Features
-------------
- Signed arbitrary-precision integer arithmetic:
  * Assignment and type conversions (i32, u32)
  * Full comparison suite (cmp, cmpabs, predicates)
  * Addition and subtraction (including scalar variants)
  * Multiplication (generic + BMI2 optimized)
  * Squaring with dedicated implementation
  * Truncated division (reciprocal-based for single-limb divisors)

- Binary import/export API with little-endian magnitude buffers
- Fit-check predicates for u8/u16/u32/u64 and i8/i16/i32/i64

Performance Optimizations
-------------------------
- Runtime CPU feature detection with algorithm dispatch
- BMI2-optimized multiplication on x86 (Karatsuba threshold: 32 limbs)
- AVX2-optimized doubling operation (threshold: 16 limbs)
- Reciprocal-based single-limb division (Granlund-Montgomery algorithm)
- Scalar multiplication fast paths (arbint_mul_i32, arbint_mul_u32)
- Early-exit optimizations for special values (-1, 0, 1)

Platform Support
----------------
Verified on:
- Linux: x86-64, arm64, i386, riscv64, s390x, ppc64le
- macOS: x86-64, arm64
- Windows: x86-64, i686 (MinGW-GCC, TCC, MSVC)

Compilers: GCC, Clang, TCC, MSVC

Build System
------------
- Autotools with shared/static library support
- pkg-config integration for easy linking
- Optional LTO support via `--enable-lto=auto|yes|no`
- Tunable optimization levels (`--with-base-optimization=default|tuned`)
- Comprehensive unit and stochastic tests via `make check`

Documentation
-------------
- Complete man page (c-arbint.3) documenting all exported APIs
- Example code demonstrating library usage
- Inline documentation for public API in arbint.h

Known Limitations
-----------------
- String conversion (arbint_set_str, arbint_get_str) not yet implemented
- Floor/ceiling division variants planned for future releases
- Some CI configurations disabled due to compiler issues (noted in README)
